# GitHub + changelog workflow (HC-Iron-Legacy)

Remote: `https://github.com/Dralorex/HC-Iron-Legacy.git`

## Goals

- Push work to GitHub often so the dev can review in real time (commits, PRs, diffs).
- Keep **`CHANGELOG.md`** updated in the same PR/commit series as code changes.

## Branching

- **`main`** — stable; merge only after dev review (or agreed quick fixes).
- **`develop`** or **`feature/<short-name>`** — day-to-day work; push here and open a **Pull Request** into `main`.

## On every meaningful change

1. Edit code.
2. Add a bullet under **`CHANGELOG.md` → [Unreleased]** (Added / Changed / Fixed).
3. If the change is user-visible or release-worthy, bump **`pom.xml`** `<version>` (single source of truth for plugin version).
4. Commit with a clear message, e.g. `fix: border shrink tick when arena empty`.
5. Push: `git push -u origin <branch>`.
6. Open or update a **Pull Request** on GitHub; dev reviews there.

## Releasing a version

1. Move `[Unreleased]` entries into a new section: `## [x.y.z] — YYYY-MM-DD` (version = `pom.xml`).
2. Leave an empty `[Unreleased]` section at the top.
3. Merge PR to `main`, then tag: `git tag v1.21.4-a0.3.1` and `git push origin v1.21.4-a0.3.1` (optional GitHub Release from the tag).

## Do not commit

- Secrets (tokens, `.env`, local DB passwords).
- Build output (`target/`) unless the repo already tracks it (prefer `.gitignore`).

## When the user asks to "push to GitHub" or "update changelog"

- Update **`CHANGELOG.md`** first or in the same commit as the code.
- Push the current branch; remind them to open/update the PR if not on `main`.
